WEBVTT

NOTE A positive slope and two intercepts. English captions; text is the exact narration script.

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.883
For y equals two-thirds x minus two,

2
00:00:03.883 --> 00:00:08.319
the constant term places the
y-intercept at zero, negative two.

3
00:00:08.969 --> 00:00:12.733
A positive slope means
rise two for run three.

4
00:00:13.483 --> 00:00:16.450
Moving right three reaches three, zero.

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.623
This is also the x-intercept.

6
00:00:19.373 --> 00:00:21.436
You could choose a different valid point,

7
00:00:21.436 --> 00:00:24.773
such as six, two, and draw the same line.

8
00:00:25.523 --> 00:00:28.062
The graph rises as x increases.

9
00:00:28.712 --> 00:00:32.413
This abstract example has
no time or distance units.
